From ff8198058c4d7902b633727ab541ab8f7e778c52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Louvignes <olivier@mgcrea.io>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:32:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 61/62] phy: ingenic: wait 1 ms after taking the PHY out of
 reset

ingenic_usb_phy_init() releases the PHY's power-on reset, then waits
with usleep_range(300, 1000). On the HiBy R1 (X1600), dwc2's first core
reset then hung at some starts after a watchdog restart: CSFTRST never
cleared ("HANG! Soft Reset timeout GRSTCTL_CSFTRST"), the probe failed
with -EBUSY, and every later reset in that start failed too. The
failures came in runs lasting hours, and unrelated changes to the kernel
made them more or less frequent: with CONFIG_MODULES and the board's
Wi-Fi nodes added, 12 starts in 80 lost USB.

Timestamps taken with ktime_get_ns() at the POR release and before the
core reset, over those 80 starts, put the reset 468 to 508 us after the
release in all 12 failed starts, and 511 us or more in all the good
ones. The sleep usually lasts close to its 1 ms maximum, but ends after
about 400 us when another timer, most likely the tick, expires within
its range; dwc2 then takes about 80 us more before its reset. The
X1600 programming manual gives no time to wait after the release, only
that POR must be asserted for at least 10 us.

Wait at least 1 ms, about twice the longest gap that failed. With
usleep_range(1000, 2000), the same kernel kept USB in 80 starts of 80.
---
 drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c b/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c
index 9759bad..3d79329 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/ingenic/phy-ingenic-usb.c
@@ -114,7 +114,12 @@ static int ingenic_usb_phy_init(struct phy *phy)
 	usleep_range(30, 300);
 	reg = readl(priv->base + REG_USBPCR_OFFSET);
 	writel(reg & ~USBPCR_POR, priv->base + REG_USBPCR_OFFSET);
-	usleep_range(300, 1000);
+
+	/*
+	 * Give the PHY time to come out of reset: on the X1600, a core reset
+	 * less than about 0.5 ms after this hangs.
+	 */
+	usleep_range(1000, 2000);
 
 	return 0;
 }
